{{!-- The Judge's brand, worn by the person it was laid on. One partial for all three sheets that
      can show it (npc, monster, character), because "Condemned" must not come to mean three
      slightly different things depending on whose sheet you are reading.

      A <span>, never a button: nothing on the BRANDED person's sheet can lift this. Condemn says
      the mark "cannot be removed or hidden until you dismiss it", and "you" is the Judge — so the
      only control that ends it lives in their roster window (templates/dialogs/condemned.hbs), and
      offering one here would be offering a click that does nothing.

      The word is wrapped in a SPAN rather than left as a bare text node. Two reasons, and the pill
      is a flex row so both bite: an anonymous flex item cannot be targeted, and the gavel and the
      word need OPPOSITE vertical nudges to look level (see .stonetop-condemned-tag-text) — so
      there has to be something to hang the label's on. It also keeps the word one item; loose
      inline text in a flex container is split per word, which `gap` then spaces apart.

      Takes `by` (the Judge names) and `byLabel` (those names joined) from condemnedContext. --}}
<span class="stonetop-condemned-tag"
      data-tooltip="{{#if byLabel}}{{localize "stonetop.condemn.tagTooltip" who=byLabel}}{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.condemn.tagTooltipPlain"}}{{/if}}"
      data-tooltip-direction="DOWN"><i class="fas fa-gavel"></i><span class="stonetop-condemned-tag-text">{{localize "stonetop.condemn.tag"}}</span></span>
